=========
Changelog
=========

Version 1.7.1 extends the consolidated 1.7.0 main release. The 1.6.0–1.6.3 entries below
number earlier development snapshots in chronological order; they do not create
historical release tags. Legacy release dates follow main/* tags where available.

Version 1.7.1 [2026-11-14]
**************************

- DATASETS: Add fresh per-member output summaries with run/source-cycle times,
  inclusive forcing bounds, steps, actual plain/gzip paths, readiness and counts.
- DATASETS: Add atomic write_summary/read_summary and separate summary_execution
  merging keyed by member; deterministic records use member "deterministic".
- DATASETS: Validate nested extra_args recursively, skip invalid leaves with
  warnings and store them under a configurable tag_args (default "execution").
- DATASETS: Filter file_by_ensemble by observed/forecast mode and preserve the
  adjusted plan when checking outputs. Reuse compatible trusted planning history.
- RUNNER: Trace sequential member/time execution without storing handlers; write
  each member summary after its time loop, with an optional merged JSON export.
- FIX: Restore planning-only CLI flags and reusable workflow setup; support the
  supplied HMC/S3M profiles, workflow suffixes and destination collection mappings.
- FIX: Keep HMC missing-value metadata numeric, accept single-variable xarray
  Datasets and normalize numeric decoding attributes in the generic NetCDF reader.
- FIX: Adapt orchestrator field collections to the S3M writer's Dataset interface,
  preserving model field names, coordinates and units.
- ORCHESTRATOR: Preserve prior collections for one-process variable workflows,
  forward output file arguments and expand workflow-tag selection for readability.
- ORCHESTRATOR: Discover requested processes in default processing toolkits and
  optional custom locations, with reusable variable/workflow template selection.
- DOCUMENTATION: Publish edition 0.5.0 with an expandable topic/guide/section
  navigation tree, sequential execution recipes and member-summary handoff guide.
- PACKAGE: Update version, citation and build date; rename the dataset time utility
  module to lib_utils_datasets and update internal callers.
- SCOPE: Exclude the datasets_parallel test runner, generated execution artifacts
  and local external-toolkit checkouts from this release.

Version 1.7.0 [2026-11-12]
**************************

- PACKAGE: Consolidate fproofs development and the latest main changes.
- DATASETS: Add HMC/S3M dataset planning, source-cycle selection, availability
  reporting and ensemble organization. Archive the unfinished forcing composer
  and its design tests under experiments/dataset_composer/.
- WORKFLOW: Separate runner execution and dataset preparation examples; split
  deterministic/probabilistic JSON and NetCDF analyzer profiles.
- APP: Include Hydrapp map/chart browsing, execution monitoring, ensemble
  summaries, RAM history and Ruler reports, plus the Flask runner interface.
- FIX: Preserve unique RainFARM run directories and the requested NetCDF/Zarr
  writer when converting native ensemble output.
- PACKAGE: Include RainFARM integration, JSON collection exports, ICON forcing
  conversion, nested configuration fixes and corrected S3M NetCDF handling.
- DOCUMENTATION: Update README, model appendices, dataset and runner guides;
  add CITATION.cff with software citation metadata and align the Sphinx
  palette and CIMA logo with the foundation website.
- LABS: Add isolated JupyterLab setup and launch scripts with an optional
  kernel registration for an existing JupyterLab installation.
- LABS: Import the legacy HMC notebooks, scripts, configuration, helper library
  and artwork under labs/hmc, preserving original authorship and licences.
  This is an archival import; migration to current APIs is deferred.
- MIGRATION: Runner entry points and settings now live in
  workflow/runner/execution/; dataset examples live in workflow/runner/datasets/.
  Analyzer settings now use explicit deterministic/probabilistic filenames.

Version 1.6.3 (development) [2026-11-09]
****************************************

- APP: Rename the Flask dashboard to Hydrapp and add legacy HAT map/chart browsing (44922b3).
- APP: Add execution monitoring, ensemble summaries, RAM history and Ruler reports (44922b3).
- APP: Add a Flask runner interface and portable figure/memory demonstrations (44922b3).
- WORKFLOW: Add lifecycle/heartbeat records, exit tracking and JSON monitoring examples (44922b3).
- PACKAGE: Organize monitoring into common, execution and resources; integrate Ruler (44922b3).
- PACKAGE: Fix namelist, orchestration and coordinate handling; add HMC state-copy utilities (44922b3).
- TESTS: Cover monitoring, Hydrapp, RFarm, HMC/S3M namelists and orchestration (44922b3).
- DOCUMENTATION: Update component credits and consolidate Hydrapp setup (44922b3).

